/target/

# ── Machine-local agent + tooling state. NEVER tracked.
#
# The publishability bar makes this load-bearing rather than tidy: going public
# "distributes every tracked byte AND the full git history to third parties, where
# it may be cloned, cached, and indexed before anyone notices a mistake."
# Anything below is local orchestration residue with no value to a reader and a
# non-zero chance of carrying paths, pids, or session identifiers.
.ntm/
.orchestrator/
.rch-tmp/
.rch-target-*/
.ee/
.claude/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
